# Phase 1 check for inc-30ps: Creature::TouchDef (src/Values.cpp, beside
# A_CDEF) must equal A_DEF less BONUS_NATURAL, BONUS_ARMOUR and BONUS_SHIELD,
# each floored at 0. Read by tools/check_touch_defence.sh.
#
# The oracle is logs/touchdef.log, written by TouchDefProbeNote (src/Values.cpp)
# under INCURSION_TOUCHDEF_PROBE. Character::CalcValues() always runs both the
# KnownOnly and the real pass (src/Values.cpp:1821-1828), so the real pass --
# and the probe with it -- fires on every recalculation, including the ones
# chargen itself triggers. The FIRST line of the log is therefore already the
# bare-handed baseline by the time this script does anything; the LAST line is
# after armour and a shield are both worn.
#
# WHY A MAGE. chargen-mage.keys starts an orc mage with no armour and no
# shield -- confirmed against tools/fixtures/chars/elf-mage-illusions-seed1
# .sheet.txt, whose Defense Class breakdown is "(base 10, +2 Dex,
# -1 encumbrance)" with no armour or shield term. Nothing needs stripping.

@include chargen-mage.keys

# chargen-mage.keys stops on the arrival room description. Dismiss it, or the
# [w] below is eaten by the description.
ESC

w
y
@until "Things in View" ESC

# --- ARMOUR (mundane, column 15 of the acquisition prompt, src/Tables.cpp:
# 320-337). Sequence proven by tools/keys/quality-self-immune-setup.keys: the
# list shows the selected row and the row under it, so @until stops one row
# above "Leather armour" and the extra DOWN selects it. 'j' is the armour
# slot. No "Enter Item Level" prompt follows a plain leather suit. ---
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*15
@until "Leather armour" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
j
SPACE
@while "two-handed" y
b
SPACE
s
@until "Things in View" ESC

# --- SHIELD (mundane, column 16). Sequence proven by
# tools/keys/shield-penalty-small.keys: acquire, answer the item-level prompt
# with the first option, then equip by typed name from the character sheet. ---
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*16
DOWN
ENTER
a
SPACE
ESC
d
W
k i t e
ENTER
ESC

@quit
